00:55:36.980 --> 00:55:38.450
HILARY PARKER
(RECORDING): Exactly.

00:55:38.450 --> 00:55:40.880
I don't actually have
tea today, though.

00:55:40.880 --> 00:55:42.810
I've also gotten
into coffee now.

00:55:42.810 --> 00:55:43.985
ROGER PENG (RECORDING): No!

00:55:43.985 --> 00:55:45.402
HILARY PARKER
(RECORDING): I know.

00:55:45.402 --> 00:55:49.740
[LAUGHS] Maybe it'll
be coffee time?

00:55:49.740 --> 00:55:50.350
Nah.

00:55:50.350 --> 00:55:52.392
ROGER PENG (RECORDING):
That doesn't sound right.

00:55:54.580 --> 00:55:57.950
So yeah, the lead up to that
was that this podcast, in part,

00:55:57.950 --> 00:55:58.890
was we--

00:55:58.890 --> 00:56:01.867
I went to grad school where
Roger was a professor.

00:56:01.867 --> 00:56:03.200
And we have this tea time thing.

00:56:03.200 --> 00:56:06.200
And we had all these
conversations, enjoyed them.

00:56:06.200 --> 00:56:08.600
And then it was like,
oh, no, I'm into coffee.

00:56:08.600 --> 00:56:10.220
Yes, we can no
longer have tea time.

00:56:10.220 --> 00:56:10.840
Yeah.

00:56:10.840 --> 00:56:13.010
This is where Hilary switches.

00:56:13.010 --> 00:56:13.600
[LAUGHTER]

00:56:13.600 --> 00:56:14.646
Yeah.

00:56:14.646 --> 00:56:18.100
And it really was
post-grad school, because--

00:56:18.100 --> 00:56:19.970
this is a long rant.

00:56:19.970 --> 00:56:21.630
You have only two minutes.

00:56:21.630 --> 00:56:24.530
Most of my life,
I had bad coffee.

00:56:24.530 --> 00:56:26.110
Like, I think we all--

00:56:26.110 --> 00:56:30.640
someone was-- the
guy from Australia

00:56:30.640 --> 00:56:33.410
was talking about how
it's an experience

00:56:33.410 --> 00:56:35.900
