drinking things on podcasts.

00:57:00.840 --> 00:57:03.923
Yeah, like you go
on a kind of long rant

00:57:03.923 --> 00:57:05.840
about listening to other
podcasts and the fact

00:57:05.840 --> 00:57:08.020
that they're talking about
the bourbon they drink.

00:57:08.020 --> 00:57:08.645
That's right.

00:57:08.645 --> 00:57:11.060
And you were like, that
doesn't belong on a podcast.

00:57:11.060 --> 00:57:12.170
Like, you were harsh.

00:57:12.170 --> 00:57:13.837
Because I thought you
were saying people

00:57:13.837 --> 00:57:17.480
shouldn't actively be
drinking alcohol on a podcast.

00:57:17.480 --> 00:57:19.550
And you were like, no,
no, no, but like talking

00:57:19.550 --> 00:57:20.720
about the bourbon.

00:57:20.720 --> 00:57:22.890
It's really annoying
when people-- yeah, anyway.

00:57:22.890 --> 00:57:25.160
Anyway, so since then--

00:57:25.160 --> 00:57:27.930
We can't say cause
and effect here,

00:57:27.930 --> 00:57:30.770
but the number of
instances has gone up--

00:57:30.770 --> 00:57:32.150
Has gone up, yeah.

00:57:32.150 --> 00:57:34.150
But literally--

00:57:34.150 --> 00:57:35.660
This will be the
hill we die on.

00:57:35.660 --> 00:57:36.340
Yeah.

00:57:36.340 --> 00:57:41.400
And the last piece of follow-up
is that based on feedback,

00:57:41.400 --> 00:57:45.100
I was open to it, I got this
mocha pot to make coffee.

00:57:45.100 --> 00:57:45.770
That's right.

00:57:45.770 --> 00:57:47.150
And I literally
couldn't give it away.

00:57:47.150 --> 00:57:48.410
Like, we had a whole episode--

00:57:48.410 --> 00:57:49.040
That's right.

00:57:49.040 --> 00:57:51.853
--about if anyone
here wanted it,

00:57:51.853 --> 00:57:53.020
I'm willing to give it away.

00:57:53.020 --> 00:57:54.145
And no one emailed us.

00:57:54.145 --> 00:57:54.770
That's right.

00:57:54.770 --> 00:57:55.895
No one wants the mocha pot.

00:57:55.895 --> 00:57:57.380
No one wants the mocha pot.

00:57:57.380 --> 00:57:59.300
And then last night, we
got some more feedback

00:57:59.300 --> 00:58:00.530
about a new device to try.

00:58:00.530 --> 00:58:01.155
That's right.

00:58:01.155 --> 00:58:03.660
Episode 102, we'll talk about.

00:58:03.660 --> 00:58:04.710
So anyway, yeah.

00:58:04.710 --> 00:58:06.980
If you don't like
coffee, don't talk to us.

00:58:06.980 --> 00:58:07.930
[LAUGHTER]

00:58:07.930 --> 00:58:09.950
We're going to keep on going.

00:58:09.950 --> 00:58:13.700
Yeah, so anyway-- actually,
I did have a tie-in for this.

00:58:13.700 --> 00:58:18.800
I was thinking about it,
where Shop Class as Soulcraft,

00:58:18.800 --> 00:58:21.980
where it's kind of like,
you just have to do stuff.

00:58:21.980 --> 00:58:23.598
Like, I started
making coffee and then

00:58:23.598 --> 00:58:24.890
I wanted to talk about it more.

00:58:24.890 --> 00:58:26.120
You know what I mean?

00:58:26.120 --> 00:58:28.400
The more that you do
something, you can kind of

00:58:28.400 --> 00:58:29.960
fall in love with anything.

00:58:29.960 --> 00:58:32.390
And you just have
to do it a bunch.

00:58:32.390 --> 00:58:33.860
And you start to care about it.

00:58:33.860 --> 00:58:38.590
So again, to the creativity,
just start trying

00:58:38.590 --> 00:58:40.580
and you'll start
to like it more.

00:58:40.580 --> 00:58:43.320
And you'll start to feel more
empowered to talk about it.

00:58:43.320 --> 00:58:45.950
And then you'll bother everyone
around you by talking about it

00:58:45.950 --> 00:58:47.090
way too much.

00:58:47.090 --> 00:58:47.660
And then--

00:58:47.660 --> 00:58:49.290
And then you'll do
a keynote on RStudio.

00:58:49.290 --> 00:58:50.880
And then you'll
do a keynote on it.

00:58:50.880 --> 00:58:52.785
Anyway, so that's our episode.

